  /* Technology & Innovation products (9 Oct 2026, Ross's library picks). Settings screen (Reach Horizon): the
     window's three dots hop in turn, as a page loading, then the cog turns a little on its hub and back while
     the hub pings (each arc trims back to its start and redraws, as the sensor arcs in Subsea telemetry). The
     cog sits in a slot: its legs end on a flat line (y 67.09) in the artwork, so a still wrapper clips it there
     and the turning legs are cut along that line instead of swinging down into the window's bottom edge. */
  :is(.pictogram--settings-screen, .pictogram--reach-pilot, .pictogram--satellite) {
    --pg-cycle: 3.2s;
  }
  .pictogram--settings-screen.is-playing .pg-dot--a { animation-name: pg-hz-dot-a; }
